note bce fixture written-nested: the write of i comes after a nested if block in the same body; the scan
note must count the if so it does not stop at the if's end. Kept, exit 103. A scan that ignores nesting
note stops at the inner end, misses the write and erases the check.
global a ulong 64
global b ulong 64
fn main to int
for i ulong 64
put a i i
put b i 200
end
s = ulong 0
for i ulong 64
if eq i 1000
s = ulong 1
end
i = add i 2
s = add s get a i
end
ret int rem s 256
end
